I'm using a bones sharing client. Well, my game (I play wizrds most of
the time and this was no exception) was fairly normal until I got to
minetown; I managed to get poison resistence early on which probably
saved my life -- about four recent attempts YASD'd from the instakill.
One of these which fell on poisoned spikes left a grave with a bag of
holding, plus some rings and wands of fire and lightening. These came
in very handy for permanent elbereth squares.

Anyways I'm in minetown about level 9, and I take a lot of damage
because of crappy AC (I hadn't found ANY armour yet) so I was playing
very carefully with a lot of elbereths. First thing I see is one of my
graves... an old one which I can't remember laying. I'm careful not to
get burdened with the stuff, which turns out to be wise as I find
myself fighting a LOT of opponents, and strong ones; the disparity
with the level before is clear. I find another grave, from somone
else, another wizard. At this point I find an orc which is terribly
well equipped - with a cloak of magic resistence, no less - who
suddenly reads a cursed scroll of summon monster which totally hems me
in; I came pretty close to dying and only elbereth and praying saved
me. I also would have been lost if I hadn't noticed at the last moment
that all of my spells weren't hurting that orc.

I eventually clear the monsters, after a lot of work, and I have to
pile all of the armor and items up on E-squares to prevent more
creatures from picking it up. And there is a LOT of stuff: at the last
count I find four graves (a samourai and three wizards). I spend a
long careful night piling up stuff in safe zones where monsters won't
get at it, writing spellbooks of identify and remove curse with magic
markers, practising remove curse until I can uncurse my entire
inventory, then finally sorting through all the stuff. Final synopsis:
I end up with Mjollnir, more than half of all the rings, scrolls and
wands identified, lots of spells, three magic markers (two of them
full to literally 99 and 98) and a pile of cloaks of magic resistence
in case I lose one. Phew... that was a hell of a lot of work, but I'm
looking pretty good right now.


